      "metadata": {
        "title": "Care for some CAViaR?",
        "posted_on": "2026-09-17",
        "last_update": "2026-09-17",
        "abstract": "Value-at-Risk is generally estimated indirectly, either from historical observations or from an assumed distribution of returns. Conditional Autoregressive Value-at-Risk (\"CAViaR\") takes a different approach by modelling the conditional quantile—and therefore VaR—directly. In this post, we introduce the main CAViaR specifications, discuss their calibration, and compare their output against a common Filtered Historical Simulations approach.\n",
        "draft": false
      },
